From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:03:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: forbid spatial reuse when BSS colour is disabled

With he_bss_color_enabled off, hostapd.uc and mac80211.sh leave out
he_spr_sr_control, so the beacon carries no Spatial Reuse Parameter Set
element. 802.11ax then lets a non-AP STA use non-SRG OBSS PD spatial
reuse with an OBSS PD level up to -62 dBm, and without a colour it
cannot tell this BSS's PPDUs from another BSS's. A client that does so
ignores the AP's frames below that level: it never takes the AP's CTS
or BlockAck, keeps retrying, and its uplink stalls a few seconds into
every association while the link still shows good signal.

Seen with a Galaxy S23 Ultra on an Arista C-360 (ath11k, IPQ8074), 5 GHz
HE40, colour disabled, the phone at -76 to -81 dBm: 2-5 frames per 15 s
reached the AP and no pings got through. With the SR Parameter Set
advertised as 3 (PSR and non-SRG OBSS PD disallowed) and colour still
disabled, the same phone sent 30-96 frames per 15 s and pinged without
loss. With colour enabled the element is already sent, and nothing
changes.

Keep the SR Parameter Set, with PSR and non-SRG OBSS PD disallowed,
whenever the colour is disabled.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/Makefile b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/Makefile
--- a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/Makefile
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 
 PKG_NAME:=wifi-scripts
 PKG_VERSION:=1.0
-PKG_RELEASE:=7
+PKG_RELEASE:=8
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0
 
 PKG_MAINTAINER:=Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
diff --git a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless/mac80211.sh b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless/mac80211.sh
--- a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless/mac80211.sh
+++ b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless/mac80211.sh
@@ -504,6 +504,11 @@
 			append base_cfg "he_spr_sr_control=$he_spr_sr_control" "$N"
 		else
 			append base_cfg "he_bss_color_disabled=1" "$N"
+			# Without a colour, clients can't tell this BSS's PPDUs from
+			# another's, so forbid them spatial reuse. With no SR Parameter
+			# Set at all they may use non-SRG OBSS PD up to -62 dBm, and
+			# ignore this AP's weaker frames as an OBSS's.
+			append base_cfg "he_spr_sr_control=3" "$N"
 		fi
 
 
diff --git a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files-ucode/usr/share/ucode/wifi/hostapd.uc b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files-ucode/usr/share/ucode/wifi/hostapd.uc
--- a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files-ucode/usr/share/ucode/wifi/hostapd.uc
+++ b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files-ucode/usr/share/ucode/wifi/hostapd.uc
@@ -458,6 +458,14 @@
 				'he_spr_srg_obss_pd_min_offset', 'he_spr_srg_obss_pd_max_offset',
 				'he_spr_srg_bss_colors', 'he_spr_srg_partial_bssid'
 			]);
+		} else {
+			/* Without a colour, clients can't tell this BSS's PPDUs
+			 * from another's, so forbid them spatial reuse. With no SR
+			 * Parameter Set at all they may use non-SRG OBSS PD up to
+			 * -62 dBm, and ignore this AP's weaker frames as an OBSS's.
+			 */
+			config.he_spr_sr_control = 3;
+			append_vars(config, [ 'he_spr_sr_control' ]);
 		}
 
 		if (!(he_phy_cap[3] & 0x80))
